#
# The Swift names of the classes these headers declare, installed beside
# them in Foundation.framework/Headers, where the compiler looks for a
# framework's API notes.
#
# Swift drops the NS prefix from some of Foundation's classes and not
# others -- ProcessInfo, but NSString and NSURL, which have value types of
# those names -- and which is which is not something the compiler works
# out: Foundation's API notes say so class by class.  Without them
# NSProcessInfo stays NSProcessInfo and every Package.swift that says
# ProcessInfo fails to compile.  Only the classes here that Swift renames
# are listed.
#
# The same file says which classes bridge to Swift's own types, and the
# importer maps NSString *, NSArray * and NSDictionary * in a signature to
# String, Array and Dictionary only because it does.  Without it the
# conformances in Swift.subproj's interface load and change nothing:
# ProcessInfo.processInfo.environment stays an NSDictionary.  Only the
# three the interface declares are here.
---
Name: Foundation
Classes:
- Name: NSArray
  SwiftBridge: Swift.Array
- Name: NSDictionary
  SwiftBridge: Swift.Dictionary
- Name: NSString
  SwiftBridge: Swift.String
- Name: NSBundle
  SwiftName: Bundle
- Name: NSFileHandle
  SwiftName: FileHandle
- Name: NSFileManager
  SwiftName: FileManager
- Name: NSInputStream
  SwiftName: InputStream
- Name: NSOutputStream
  SwiftName: OutputStream
- Name: NSProcessInfo
  SwiftName: ProcessInfo
- Name: NSStream
  SwiftName: Stream
- Name: NSUserDefaults
  SwiftName: UserDefaults
